Hi HN,<p>I&#x27;ve been building SaaS products for more than 20 years, and lately I&#x27;ve been thinking a lot about how we interact with software.<p>When we add a feature, we have to figure out where it goes in the UI and how users will interact with it. Then users have to learn our particular way of doing something.<p>AI lets us flip that around: the software can translate what the user wants into the actions needed to accomplish it.<p>Yedric lets devs add a natural-language interface to an existing SaaS app. You expose your app&#x27;s actions and give it your docs and user context. Users can then ask for things like:<p>• &quot;Export the table to a CSV&quot;
• &quot;Fix this disconnected integration&quot;
• &quot;Change my logo color to #B5E2F4&quot;<p>We originally built Yedric for our own Shopify apps and discovered an interesting side effect: the conversations became a useful source of product feedback. One of our apps surfaced 80+ distinct feature requests this way last month.<p>Yedric uses a small JS SDK and MCP to connect to your app&#x27;s capabilities. It&#x27;s free, you bring your own LLM key, and you can get a basic implementation running in under 30 minutes. Let me know how you like it!
